#{[17592186569934 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569934 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569934 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569934 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569934 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569934 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569934 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569934 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186569785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569934 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "dc076be1-fa1d-5a8e-9f7b-f0d944a99952" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569963 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186569890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569963 #edb/ref 1069 "q-88457" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569963 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569963 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the product of solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}{e}^{3x}-4x{e}^{3x}-12{e}^{3x}=0?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569963 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "12b67edd-e409-5ea0-9859-9fa94b363ebb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569963 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}-4x{e}^{3x}-12{e}^{3x} & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-4x-12){e}^{3x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-4x-12=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{e}^{3x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}-4x-12=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x+2)(x-6)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-2,6.$\n\n- The equation ${e}^{3x}=0$ has no solutions because ${e}^{3x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-2,6,$ and their product is $(-2)\\cdot 6=-12.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569977 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186569870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569977 #edb/ref 1069 "q-100799" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569977 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569977 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the product of solutions of the equation $9{x}^{2}{e}^{x}=36{e}^{x}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569977 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3499241b-bbd1-5943-8b7b-1fe387959bfa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569977 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}{e}^{x} & =36{e}^{x} \\\\ 9{x}^{2}{e}^{x}-36{e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ (9{x}^{2}-36){e}^{x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}-36=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{e}^{x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $9{x}^{2}-36=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(3x+6)(3x-6)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-2,2.$\n\n- The equation ${e}^{x}=0$ has no solutions because ${e}^{x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-2,2,$ and their product is $(-2)\\cdot 2=-4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570034 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186569934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570034 #edb/ref 1069 "q-100794" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570034 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570034 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the product of solutions of the equation $3{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x}=11x\\cdot {5}^{x}+4\\cdot {5}^{x}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570034 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e2c0ab81-ce73-5f44-b936-e8bb7ee9594f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570034 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we factor the equation:\n\n  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x} & =11x\\cdot {5}^{x}+4\\cdot {5}^{x} \\\\ 3{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x}-11x\\cdot {5}^{x}-4\\cdot {5}^{x} & =0 \\\\ (3{x}^{2}-11x-4)\\cdot {5}^{x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}-11x-4=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{5}^{x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $3{x}^{2}-11x-4=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(3x+1)(x-4)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-\\frac{1}{3},4.$\n\n- The equation ${5}^{x}=0$ has no solutions because ${5}^{x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-\\frac{1}{3},4,$ and their product is $(-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 4=-\\frac{4}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570045 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186570058 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570045 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "114fb63f-63fb-5356-b093-291fb3d3fff9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570045 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186292661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570058 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4b9091a4-a0a1-5587-b592-b4fc29ebd434" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570058 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186292664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570061 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186570081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570061 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "59d17a34-18a9-5f21-9ce9-f181a0fe6f9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570061 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186569963 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570081 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186570092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570081 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b0acc92f-1dde-5ca1-888f-6358a324a4bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570081 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186570034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570092 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186570045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570092 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d4980d2a-a8b8-5708-868f-e424629b107f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570092 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186569977 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
